I would like to dedicate my ascension to the memory of my Uncle Glen, 
who died on Sunday from a heart attack. I was bound and determined to 
win one for him.

I started a gnome healer and named my cat Squeaky. I leveled Squeaky up 
by not engaging any of the monsters, then ran down to minetown while 
still level 1. The priest gratefully accepted my gold and my AC went 
down to 3. Minetown also had some good spellbooks - one was a spellbook 
of identify, but it was very difficult to cast. I tried on a ring that I 
managed to identify as uncursed on the altar and Squeaky hauled off and 
bit me! I quickly pulled it off and named it conflict.

Back to the main dungeon. I lost Squeaky somewhere, somehow, either to a 
  trap door or some monster killed her. I doubt she was killed, because 
I never got a message about a sad feeling, but we got permanently 
separated. I used an elvish dagger and some decent armor I found to 
survive. Unfortunately I only ever found about 5 daggers. The RNG was 
very skimpy on those. I got by mainly on good AC and conflict.

That held out until a nasty fight with a jaguar. I burned a scroll of 
teleportation, only to wind up about 6 squares from the beast. For 
whatever reason the jaguar decided to break off hostilities and run for 
it, too - but I knew it would be back. I took the opportunity to lock 
the door of the room I was in and recuperate.

So there I am trying to id my stuff when, despite an 80% failure rate, I 
got a full id. And sitting right in my inventory was a wand of wishing. 
Suddenly, it was a different game.

I got some GDSM, Magicbane (I was expert in daggers and I like Magicbane 
in the end game), a helm of brilliance (to make spellcasting easier), 
speed boots and an amulet of reflection (I got a BoH from Sokoban). My 
AC was now -17 and I had a very decent artifact weapon, which was good 
because despite several sacfests Hermes never gave me a weapon. In 
retrospect I wish I had wished for a robe, but wound up using a cloak of 
protection I found.

Back to the mines. Along the way I find a spellbook of charm monster, 
which gives opportunities to replace Squeaky. At one point I charmed a 
vampire lord and named him Dracula. Unfortunately, Dracula was very 
uncooperative at following me around and it got tedious waiting several 
hundred turns for him to show up at the stairs, so I ditched him in 
mine's end.

I plodded along in the main dungeon and found the entrance to Ft. 
Ludios. What the heck - I have reflection and magic resistance, why not 
loot the place? So I did. I came out with about 24,000gp (I didnt take 
all the gold) and in truth it served no purpose but to occasionally 
burden me. I had already given enough gold to the priests to get an 
intrinsic AC of 0 and further donations were largely a waste of time.

Cyclops was a complete pushover, although he did manage to drain a few 
levels. I polypiled a bunch of rings and got a ring of levitation. This 
allowed me to get across to Medusa's island and do her in.

The castle was a joke - I put on my ring of conflict and let them go at 
one another. I got the other wand and wished for 2 blessed scrolls of 
genocide (to get rid of liches and mind flayers) and another magic 
marker to put the finishing touches on my armor.

The rest of the game went by the book, with the most interesting thing 
happening was a vampire who read a scroll of create monster while 
confused and littered Vlad's tower with acid blobs. I had to face Rodney 
7 times (I always get a kick how he says "fool! thou dost think you 
could kill me?" when the answer is "yes, especially when I am holding a 
c corpse in my gloved hand and you are dressed in a robe.").

The astral plane was more an annoyance than anything - I had 223 hp 
total and I dont think I ever dropped under 190. The altar to Hermes was 
the 2nd one I visited.

Woot!


